{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"authorities\":[{\"dependency_id\":\"missing.fc4356b7b5dda202cfa18c37\",\"evidence\":{\"quote\":\"Paragraph 4.3 of the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct) and paragraph 11.10 of the Guidelines for Virtual Asset Trading Platform Operators (VATP Guidelines).\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u66.13108\"},\"needed_for_control\":true,\"title_or_locator\":\"Code of Conduct paragraph 4.3; VATP Guidelines paragraph 11.10\"},{\"dependency_id\":\"missing.8a249b39a6219ee7a14a19cf\",\"evidence\":{\"quote\":\"Please also refer to paragraph 20 of the SFC’s circular “Detection and prevention of potential layering activities in money laundering” issued on 17 November 2025.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u68.13360\"},\"needed_for_control\":true,\"title_or_locator\":\"SFC circular “Detection and prevention of potential layering activities in money laundering”, paragraph 20, 17 November 2025\"}],\"claims\":[{\"action\":\"contact the named SFC staff member for assistance with queries regarding the circular\",\"actor\":\"Person with queries regarding the circular\",\"claim_id\":\"c1\",\"conditions\":[\"Queries concern this circular.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Should you have any queries regarding this circular, please contact Ms Kiki Wong at 2231 1569 for assistance.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u49.12039\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"PERMISSION\",\"modality\":\"MAY\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"A person with queries regarding the circular may contact Ms Kiki Wong at 2231 1569 for assistance.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"provide the circular\",\"actor\":\"Intermediaries Division, Securities and Futures Commission\",\"claim_id\":\"c2\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Intermediaries Division\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u50.12152\"},{\"quote\":\"Securities and Futures Commission\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u52.12179\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"SCOPE\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"The source identifies the Intermediaries Division of the Securities and Futures Commission as the issuing context.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"enable a payer to pre-authorise a bank account held in the payer’s own name to be debited by direct debit payments initiated by the payee\",\"actor\":\"eDDA service under the Faster Payment System\",\"claim_id\":\"c3\",\"conditions\":[\"The account is held in the payer’s own name.\",\"The payments are direct debit payments initiated by the payee.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"1   eDDA is a service under the Faster Payment System which enables a payer to pre-authorise a bank account held in the payer’s own name to be debited by direct debit payments initiated by the payee.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u56.12241\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"DEFINITION\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"eDDA is defined as a Faster Payment System service enabling a payer to pre-authorise the payer’s own-name bank account for payee-initiated direct-debit payments.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"initiate eDDA setup requests\",\"actor\":\"Payer or payee\",\"claim_id\":\"c4\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"For the avoidance of doubt, eDDA instructions may be initiated either by the payer or by the payee:\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u58.12455\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"PERMISSION\",\"modality\":\"MAY\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"eDDA instructions may be initiated by either the payer or the payee.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"initiate eDDA setup requests through their own banks\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms’ clients acting as payers under a standard eDDA arrangement\",\"claim_id\":\"c5\",\"conditions\":[\"The arrangement is standard eDDA.\",\"The client is acting as payer.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(a)  under a standard eDDA arrangement, licensed firms’ clients, as payers, initiate eDDA setup requests through their own banks;\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u60.12562\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"SCOPE\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTEXT\",\"statement\":\"Under standard eDDA, licensed-firm clients as payers initiate setup requests through their own banks.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"initiate eDDA setup requests on the basis of payer pre-authorisation and information\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms acting as payees under a simplified eDDA arrangement\",\"claim_id\":\"c6\",\"conditions\":[\"The arrangement is simplified eDDA.\",\"The clients act as payers.\",\"Pre-authorisation and information are provided by the clients.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"(b)  under a simplified eDDA arrangement, licensed firms, as payees, initiate eDDA setup requests on the basis of pre-authorisation and information provided by their clients, as payers.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u62.12703\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"For simplified eDDA, licensed firms acting as payees should initiate setup requests based on pre-authorisation and information supplied by their payer clients.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"apply the circular’s simplified-eDDA guidance\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c7\",\"conditions\":[\"The processing concerns a new simplified eDDA setup request.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"This circular focuses on simplified eDDA arrangements. For details on the differences between standard eDDA and simplified eDDA, please refer to the website of Hong Kong Interbank Clearing Limited.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u64.12896\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"SCOPE\",\"modality\":\"DESCRIPTIVE\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The circular’s scope is simplified eDDA arrangements; differences from standard eDDA require reference to the Hong Kong Interbank Clearing Limited website.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"The supplied piece does not provide the website details or the full simplified-eDDA requirements.\"]},{\"action\":\"have regard to applicable limits on the number of bank accounts a client may designate for deposits and withdrawals, including accounts linked through eDDA setup requests\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c8\",\"conditions\":[\"Processing new eDDA setup requests.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"For the avoidance of doubt, when processing new eDDA setup requests, licensed firms should have regard to the applicable limits on the number of bank accounts that a client may designate for deposits and withdrawals, including bank accounts linked through eDDA setup requests.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u68.13360\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"When processing new eDDA setup requests, licensed firms should consider applicable limits on client-designated deposit and withdrawal accounts, including eDDA-linked accounts.\",\"temporal\":[\"When processing new eDDA setup requests\"],\"uncertainty\":[\"The applicable numerical or other limits are not supplied.\"]},{\"action\":\"subject designated accounts to the same bank-account registration mechanism implemented by the licensed firm\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c9\",\"conditions\":[\"Accounts are designated for deposits or withdrawals, including through eDDA setup requests.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Such accounts should be subject to the same bank account registration mechanism implemented by the licensed firm.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u68.13360\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Designated deposit or withdrawal accounts, including eDDA-linked accounts, should undergo the licensed firm’s same bank-account registration mechanism.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"The mechanism’s specific requirements are not supplied.\"]},{\"action\":\"refrain from accepting the initial deposit through simplified eDDA\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c10\",\"conditions\":[\"Clients were onboarded via the “online onboarding of clients using a designated bank account in Hong Kong” approach.\",\"The firm is not satisfied that the eDDA setup request is authorised by the bank account owner.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"For the avoidance of doubt, for clients onboarded via the “online onboarding of clients using a designated bank account in Hong Kong” approach, licensed firms should refrain from accepting the initial deposit through simplified eDDA arrangements unless they are satisfied that the eDDA setup request is authorised by the bank account owner.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u70.13929\"}],\"exceptions\":[\"Acceptance is permitted only if the firm is satisfied that the setup request is authorised by the bank account owner.\"],\"kind\":\"PROHIBITION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD_NOT\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"For clients onboarded through the specified online designated-bank-account approach, licensed firms should not accept the initial deposit via simplified eDDA unless satisfied that the bank account owner authorised the setup request.\",\"temporal\":[\"At acceptance of the initial deposit\"],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"refrain from relying solely on client-provided deposit record documents to ascertain bank account ownership\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c11\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms should refrain from relying solely on deposit record documents provided by clients to ascertain bank account ownership.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u72.14284\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"PROHIBITION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD_NOT\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Licensed firms should not determine bank-account ownership solely from deposit-record documents supplied by clients.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[]},{\"action\":\"apply customer-due-diligence and identification requirements\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c12\",\"conditions\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Chapter 5 and Chapter 7 of the Guideline on Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Financing of Terrorism (For Licensed Corporations and SFC-licensed Virtual Asset Service Providers).\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u74.14433\"}],\"exceptions\":[],\"kind\":\"DEPENDENCY\",\"modality\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"The source points to Chapters 5 and 7 of the AML/ CFT Guideline as relevant requirements, but this piece does not state their substantive checks.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"The referenced chapters are not provided, so exact identification or authorisation checks cannot be determined from this piece alone.\"]},{\"action\":\"notify the SFC\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c13\",\"conditions\":[\"The notification obligations are relevant and applicable.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms are also reminded of their notification obligations to the SFC under paragraph 12.5 of the Code of Conduct and paragraph 16.7 of the VATP Guidelines, where relevant and applicable.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u76.14626\"}],\"exceptions\":[\"Only where relevant and applicable.\"],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"MUST\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Licensed firms must comply with applicable SFC notification obligations under Code of Conduct paragraph 12.5 and VATP Guidelines paragraph 16.7.\",\"temporal\":[],\"uncertainty\":[\"The triggering events and content of notification are not supplied.\"]},{\"action\":\"review and, where necessary, amend client agreements and promptly notify clients of related changes\",\"actor\":\"Licensed firms\",\"claim_id\":\"c14\",\"conditions\":[\"Changes are necessary in light of the firm’s risk-mitigating measures.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Licensed firms should review and, where necessary, amend their client agreements to ensure they remain appropriate in light of their risk mitigating measures, and promptly notify clients of any related changes.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u78.14836\"}],\"exceptions\":[\"Amendment is required only where necessary.\"],\"kind\":\"OBLIGATION\",\"modality\":\"SHOULD\",\"relevance\":\"CONTROL\",\"statement\":\"Licensed firms should review client agreements, amend them when necessary to remain appropriate to risk-mitigation measures, and promptly notify clients of related changes.\",\"temporal\":[\"Promptly after related changes\"],\"uncertainty\":[]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"The piece does not supply the detailed account-owner authorisation or identification methods required by the referenced Code of Conduct, VATP Guidelines, AML/CFT Guideline, or other SFC circular.\",\"Applicable account-number limits and the firm’s bank-account registration mechanism are unspecified.\",\"The supplied facts do not state whether the client used the specified online onboarding approach, whether the request is authorised by the bank account owner, or whether notification obligations are relevant and applicable; therefore a determinate processing decision cannot be made.\"],\"units\":[{\"claim_ids\":[\"c1\"],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Contact information only; it does not impose processing controls.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u49.12039\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c2\"],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Issuer/department identifiers.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u50.12152\"},{\"claim_ids\":[\"c2\"],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Issuing authority identifier.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u52.12179\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"disposition\":\"CONTEXT\",\"rationale\":\"Document terminator with no substantive proposition.\",\"unit_id\":\"dbbbc321f6397.u53.12214\"},{\"claim_ids\":[],\"d